    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present this bright and well-presented three-bedroom mid-terrace family home to the market, ideally positioned within the mature and ever-popular Glenties Park development in Finglas, Dublin 11. No. 27 enjoys a peaceful cul-de-sac setting and is sure to appeal to a wide range of buyers, including first-time purchasers, growing families and investors alike.\nThe location is second to none, with every conceivable amenity within easy reach. Finglas Village, Charlestown Shopping Centre, and Clearwater Shopping Centre are all nearby, while a host of excellent primary and secondary schools, parks, cafés, and sporting facilities are within walking distance. The area is exceptionally well connected with excellent bus routes servicing Dublin City Centre, together with easy access to the M50, Dublin Airport and Dublin City University.\nBright and well laid out internal living accommodation of c. 75 sq. m. comprises of an entrance hallway, a spacious open-plan living and dining area, a fully fitted kitchen, three well-proportioned bedrooms with fitted wardrobes and a fully tiled family shower room. To the rear, the property further benefits from a fully self-contained unit complete with a kitchen, double bedroom and en-suite, offering a variety of potential uses subject to the purchaser's own requirements.\nNo. 27 comes to the market in good condition throughout and benefits from gas fired central heating, double glazed windows, and a sunny south-facing rear garden. The property is presented with vacant possession, allowing the successful purchaser to move in immediately with no onward chain.\nThis is a fantastic opportunity to acquire a spacious home with the bonus of versatile additional accommodation in one of Finglas' most established residential locations. Early viewing is highly advised. Contact Ray Cooke Auctioneers today on 086 832 3302 or 01 541 1455 to arrange a viewing.\n\nKey Features\n• BER D2\n• c. 75 sq.m.\n• Built in 1977\n• Gas fired central heating\n• Double glazed windows\n• Bright and spacious living accommodation\n• Fully fitted kitchen\n• Built-in wardrobes\n• South-facing rear garden\n• Fully self-contained unit to the rear\n• Rear unit with kitchen, double bedroom and en-suite\n• Vacant possession\n• Quiet cul-de-sac location\n• Mature and highly sought-after development\n• Excellent schools and local amenities nearby\n• Easy access to M50, Dublin Airport and Dublin City Centre\n• Ideal for first-time buyers, families and investors\n• Early viewing highly advised"
      },
      {
